{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-968785ae7de13d6a","type":"tool_result","content":"437\t\n438\t// splitBody splits a markdown body into a preamble (text before the first \"## \"\n439\t// heading line) and an ordered list of sections. A heading line is a line\n440\t// starting with the exact prefix \"## \" (hash-hash-space). A bare \"---\" line is\n441\t// never a heading. Both \"\\n\" and \"\\r\\n\" line endings are tolerated: a trailing\n442\t// \"\\r\" before \"\\n\" is part of the terminator, so the heading name of the line\n443\t// \"## Parked\\r\\n\" is \"## Parked\". Returns (\"\", nil) for an empty body.\n444\tfunc splitBody(body string) (preamble string, sections []bodySection) {\n445\t\tif body == \"\" {\n446\t\t\treturn \"\", nil\n447\t\t}\n448\t\tvar preambleBuilder strings.Builder\n449\t\ttype sectionAcc struct {\n450\t\t\theading string\n451\t\t\tcontent strings.Builder\n452\t\t}\n453\t\tvar accs []sectionAcc\n454\t\tcurrent := -1\n455\t\tfor len(body) > 0 {\n456\t\t\tvar line string\n457\t\t\tif idx := strings.IndexByte(body, '\\n'); idx >= 0 {\n458\t\t\t\tline = body[:idx+1]\n459\t\t\t\tbody = body[idx+1:]\n460\t\t\t} else {\n461\t\t\t\tline = body\n462\t\t\t\tbody = \"\"\n463\t\t\t}\n464\t\t\tif _, isHeading := headingName(line); isHeading {\n465\t\t\t\taccs = append(accs, sectionAcc{heading: line})\n466\t\t\t\tcurrent = len(accs) - 1\n467\t\t\t\tcontinue\n468\t\t\t}\n469\t\t\tif current < 0 {\n470\t\t\t\tpreambleBuilder.WriteString(line)\n471\t\t\t} else {\n472\t\t\t\taccs[current].content.WriteString(line)\n473\t\t\t}\n474\t\t}\n475\t\tsections = make([]bodySection, 0, len(accs))\n476\t\tfor _, a := range accs {\n477\t\t\tsections = append(sections, bodySection{heading: a.heading, content: a.content.String()})\n478\t\t}\n479\t\treturn preambleBuilder.String(), sections\n480\t}\n481\t\n482\t// headingName returns the heading name — the heading line with its terminator\n483\t// (\"\\n\", \"\\r\\n\", or 