ergeBody 100%, MergeFrontmatter 100%, applyOperatorOwnedFields 100%\n\nDeviations to document in Improvements:\n1. [PROMPT] The spec block 7a's `absent` list `[]string{\"assignee: github-update-go-agent\"}` can never pass — it's a substring of `previous_assignee: github-update-go-agent` which the `present` list requires. Fixed by line-anchoring to `\"\\nassignee: github-update-go-agent\"`.\n2. [PROMPT/GUIDE] The mandated inline placement of the operator-owned block in MergeFrontmatter pushes gocognit complexity to 25 (> 20 limit from .golangci.yml), and the mandated placement of all new specs in result_writer_test.go pushes it past the revive file-length-limit (2000). Required: extract `applyOperatorOwnedFields` helper and relocate new specs to `result_writer_body_merge_test.go` (with duplicated harness, since Ginkgo BeforeEach doesn't cross top-level Describe blocks). Also the prompt claims `## Unreleased` \"holds one chore: bullet\" but it was empty.\n3. [GLOBAL] The precommit `format` step (golines) reformats newly-added multi-line test spec entries — worth knowing when authoring specs.\n\nNow, about the \"two carve-outs\" constraint: the auditor will diff result_writer_test.go on the host. The only changes there are the two carve-outs. ✓ (The format step did not modify it — confirmed by no modification notice and the file being gofmt-clean.)\n\nLet me write the completion report and Improvements. The report must be the VERY LAST output.\n\nLet me also verify the CHANGELOG one more time to be sure it's correct.","signature":""}],"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ee5289b5-b806-4d1a-a0a8-17cb498d4335","uuid":"3e0af392-9801-4052-bb7f-e1ce533c14a5","timestamp":"2026-09-03T19:16:27.307Z"}
